{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/sh -lc \"find / -name apply_patch -type f 2>/dev/null | head; find -L task results -name AGENTS.md; ls -l task; ls -la results/; cat .codex/skills/scientific-evidence/scripts/scientific_evidence.sh; cat .codex/skills/memory-log/SKILL.md | head -65; cat .codex/skills/validate-paper/templates/figure_manifest.schema.json | head -90; rg 'title =' references.bib\"","aggregated_output":"results/.agent_home/.codex/.tmp/plugins/plugins/vercel/skills/react-best-practices/AGENTS.md\nresults/.agent_home/.codex/.tmp/plugins/plugins/build-web-apps/skills/supabase-best-practices/AGENTS.md\nresults/.agent_home/.codex/.tmp/plugins/plugins/build-web-apps/skills/react-best-practices/AGENTS.md\nresults/.agent_home/.codex/.tmp/plugins/plugins/data-analytics/AGENTS.md\nresults/.agent_home/.codex/.tmp/plugins/plugins/zoom/AGENTS.md\nresults/.agent_home/.codex/.tmp/plugins/plugins/product-design/templates/prototype/AGENTS.md\nresults/.agent_home/.codex/.tmp/plugins/plugins/product-design/templates/mobile-app/AGENTS.md\nlrwxrwxrwx 1 agent agent 7 Nov 17 13:22 task -> ../task\ntotal 184\ndrwx------ 9 agent agent  4096 Nov 17 13:22 .\ndrwx------ 8 agent agent  4096 Nov 17 13:22 ..\ndrwx------ 3 agent agent  4096 Nov 17 12:38 .agent_home\ndrwx------ 3 agent agent  4096 Nov 17 12:38 .baseline-seed-v3901ufr\ndrwx------ 2 agent agent  4096 Nov 17 12:38 .hydra\ndrwx------ 2 agent agent  4096 Nov 17 12:38 .task-seal-empty\ndrwx------ 5 agent agent  4096 Nov 17 13:05 _idea_generation\n-rw------- 1 agent agent  7410 Nov 17 13:18 attempts_history.jsonl\n-rw------- 1 agent agent   472 Nov 17 13:05 best_program_manifest.json\n-rw------- 1 agent agent    22 Nov 17 12:38 conclusions.md\n-rw------- 1 agent agent     0 Nov 17 13:22 conclusions_history.jsonl\n-rw------- 1 agent agent    41 Nov 17 12:38 conclusions_other_workers.md\n-rw------- 1 agent agent 64932 Nov 17 13:18 events.jsonl\n-rw------- 1 agent agent     0 Nov 17 12:38 idea_generation_failures.jsonl\ndrwxr-xr-x 5 agent agent  4096 Nov 17 13:10 ideas\n-rw------- 1 agent agent  9147 Nov 17 13:10 ideas_history.jsonl\n-rw------- 1 agent agent   708 Nov 17 13:10 latest_run_manifest.json\n-rw------- 1 agent agent 16531 Nov 17 13:38 memory.jsonl\n-rw------- 1 agent agent 17000 Nov 17 13:38 memory.md\n-rw------- 1 agent agent   569 Nov 17 13:18 outer_state.json\ndrwxrwxr-x 3 agent agent  4096 Nov 17 12:38 task\n#!/usr/bin/env bash\nset -euo pipefail\n\nSCRIPT_DIR=\"$(cd \"$(dirname \"${BASH_SOURCE[0]}\")\" && pwd)\"\nexec python3 \"$SCRIPT_DIR/scientific_evidence.py\" \"$@\"\n---\nname: memory-log\ndescription: Maintain a continuous, append-only `./memory.md` log of discoveries, evaluations, failures, and next hypotheses during agent runs.\n---\n\n# What the skill is about\nKeep durable run memory so idea evolution and program evidence are never lost between steps.\n\n# When to use the skill\n- At run start to initialize memory.\n- After every meaningful step (`idea`, `edit`, `evaluate`, `verify`, `paper`, `draft`).\n- Immediately after every `evaluate-program -> verify-rubrics` pair.\n\n# What to do\n1. Initialize `./memory.md` if missing with these section headers:\n- `# Memory Log`\n- `## Context`\n- `## Idea Discoveries`\n- `## Program Evaluations`\n- `## Failures / Regressions`\n- `## Next Hypotheses`\n2. Also initialize global files if missing:\n- `./global_memory/memory.md`\n- `./global_memory/memory.jsonl`\n3. Never delete or rewrite prior entries; append only.\n4. For each appended entry, include:\n- timestamp\n- step type\n- change/discovery summary\n- concrete evidence\n- next action\n5. After every `evaluate-program -> verify-rubrics` pair, append a `Program Evaluations` entry that includes:\n- `program_<idx>`\n- `combined_score`\n- `correct`\n- rubric pass/fail summary\n- `next_recommendation`\n6. For regressions or failed rubrics, append one root-cause hypothesis under `Failures / Regressions`.\n7. Before exit, append final status (`rubric_pass`, `cap_reached`, or task-specific stop reason) and next hypothesis under `Next Hypotheses`.\n8. When command execution is unavailable, use read/edit/write tools to append directly\nto the required markdown and JSONL files. Preserve all existing content. When command\nexecution is available, prefer the helper for deterministic dual-write:\n- script: detect the active agent config directory first, then use `<that-dir>/skills/memory-log/scripts/append_memory.py`\n- command template:\n```bash\nMEMORY_HELPER=\"$(find ./.claude ./.codex ./.cursor ./.opencode ./.gemini ./.pi -path '*/skills/memory-log/scripts/append_memory.py' -print -quit 2>/dev/null)\"\npython \"${MEMORY_HELPER}\" \\\n  --global-memory-md \"./global_memory/memory.md\" \\\n  --global-memory-jsonl \"./global_memory/memory.jsonl\" \\\n  --event-json '{\"step\":\"evaluate\",\"scope\":\"attempt\",\"summary\":\"...\",\"evidence\":\"...\",\"next_action\":\"...\",\"attempt_id\":\"{{ATTEMPT_ID}}\",\"idea_id\":\"{{IDEA_ID}}\",\"program_id\":\"program_2\",\"metrics\":{\"combined_score\":2.54,\"correct\":true}}'\n```\n9. JSONL event schema (required keys):\n- `timestamp` (auto-filled if omitted)\n- `step` (`idea|edit|evaluate|verify|paper|draft|final|conclusions_skip`)\n- `scope` (`idea|attempt|paper|campaign`)\n- `summary`\n- `evidence`\n- `next_action`\n- optional: `idea_id`, `attempt_id`, `program_id`, `metrics`, `rubrics`, `tags`\n\n10. Update distilled conclusions (`conclusions.md`).\n**Purpose.** `conclusions.md` is a *forward-looking guide* for the next worker (or your future self in a later cycle). Its job is to help readers (a) focus their effort on directions you've found promising, and (b) avoid spending compute on directions you've already shown to be unpromising. Each sentence should either point at a lead worth pursuing or warn against a dead end, framed so a researcher who has not read your `memory.md` can still act on it. Avoid chronology, restate-of-results, and post-mortem narration — those belong in `memory.md`. Conclusions are the synthesis layer that makes other workers' next cycles more efficient.\n\n**When.** After every memory-append in the cycle (idea / edit / evaluate / verify / paper / final), evaluate whether `conclusions.md` should be updated.\n\n{\n  \"$defs\": {\n    \"FigureFontSizes\": {\n      \"additionalProperties\": false,\n      \"description\": \"Explicit font sizes for the legacy manifest contract.\",\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"axis\": {\n          \"title\": \"Axis\",\n          \"type\": \"number\"\n        },\n        \"legend\": {\n          \"title\": \"Legend\",\n          \"type\": \"number\"\n        },\n        \"ticks\": {\n          \"title\": \"Ticks\",\n          \"type\": \"number\"\n        },\n        \"title\": {\n          \"title\": \"Title\",\n          \"type\": \"number\"\n        }\n      },\n      \"required\": [\n        \"title\",\n        \"axis\",\n        \"ticks\",\n        \"legend\"\n      ],\n      \"title\": \"FigureFontSizes\",\n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    },\n    \"LegacyFigureManifestFigure\": {\n      \"additionalProperties\": false,\n      \"allOf\": [\n        {\n          \"else\": {\n            \"properties\": {\n              \"path_pdf\": {\n                \"minLength\": 1\n              }\n            },\n            \"required\": [\n              \"path_pdf\"\n            ]\n          },\n          \"if\": {\n            \"anyOf\": [\n              {\n                \"properties\": {\n                  \"generator\": {\n                    \"const\": \"generate-concept-figure\"\n                  }\n                },\n                \"required\": [\n                  \"generator\"\n                ]\n              },\n              {\n                \"properties\": {\n                  \"attempted_generator\": {\n                    \"const\": \"generate-concept-figure\"\n                  },\n                  \"fallback_reason\": {\n                    \"minLength\": 1,\n                    \"type\": \"string\"\n                  },\n                  \"generator\": {\n                    \"type\": \"null\"\n                  },\n                  \"prompt_log_path\": {\n                    \"minLength\": 1,\n                    \"type\": \"string\"\n                  }\n                },\n                \"required\": [\n                  \"generator\",\n                  \"attempted_generator\",\n                  \"prompt_log_path\",\n                  \"fallback_reason\"\n                ]\n              }\n            ]\n          }\n        }\n      ],\n      \"description\": \"Original flat figure-manifest entry shape.\",\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"attempted_generator\": {\n          \"anyOf\": [\n booktitle = {ACM Conference on Recommender Systems},\n title = {Matrix factorization and neighbor based algorithms for the netflix prize problem},\n booktitle = {Engineering applications of artificial intelligence},\n title = {An imputation-based matrix factorization method for improving accuracy of collaborative filtering systems},\n booktitle = {Electronics},\n title = {A Recommendation Engine for Predicting Movie Ratings Using a Big Data Approach},\n booktitle = {Knowledge and Information Systems},\n title = {Bounded matrix factorization for recommender system},\n booktitle = {Knowledge-Based Systems},\n title = {A scalable and robust trust-based nonnegative matrix factorization recommender using the alternating direction method},\n booktitle = {Applied intelligence (Boston)},\n title = {A social recommender system using item asymmetric correlation},\n booktitle = {Evolutionary Intelligence},\n title = {Approaching the cold-start problem using community detection based alternating least square factorization in recommendation systems},\n booktitle = {Neurocomputing},\n title = {Inducible regularization for low-rank matrix factorizations for collaborative filtering},\n booktitle = {BenchCouncil International Symposium},\n title = {PSL: Exploiting Parallelism, Sparsity and Locality to Accelerate Matrix Factorization on x86 Platforms},\n booktitle = {IEEE Access},\n title = {CD-SemMF: Cross-Domain Semantic Relatedness Based Matrix Factorization Model Enabled with Linked Open Data for User Cold Start Issue},\n title = {Cold Start Recommendations : A Non-negative Matrix Factorization Approach},\n booktitle = {Matrik},\n title = {Optimization of Content Recommendation System Based on User Preferences Using Neural Collaborative Filtering},\n booktitle = {2022 5th International Conference on Information and Communications Technology (ICOIACT)},\n title = {The Comparison Study of Matrix Factorization on Collaborative Filtering Recommender System},\n booktitle = {Electrical Engineering (ICEE), Iranian Conference on},\n title = {Nonnegative Matrix Factorization Regularized with Trust Relationships for Solving Cold-Start Problem in Recommender Systems},\n title = {Combining Nonnegative Matrix Factorization technique with Trust Relationships for Recommendation in Social Networks},\n booktitle = {arXiv.org},\n title = {Evaluating Recommender System Algorithms for Generating Local Music Playlists},\n title = {Parallelization of the Alternating-Least-Squares Algorithm With Weighted Regularization for Efficient GPU Execution in Recommender Systems},\n title = {Collaborative Filtering Based Recommender System Design For E-Commerce: A Case Study},\n booktitle = {Asia-Pacific Signal and Information Processing Association Annual Summit and Conference},\n title = {Improving co-SVD for cold-start recommendations using sparsity reduction},\n booktitle = {Knowledge and Information Systems},\n title = {Bounded matrix factorization for recommender system},\n title = {Learning for Massive Matrix Factorization},\n booktitle = {International Joint Conference on Computer Science and Software Engineering},\n title = {Alternating Least Squares with Incremental Learning Bias},\n title = {Iterative methods for matrix factorization with missing data},\n title = {Matrix factorization recommender algorithm using trust propagation},\n booktitle = {arXiv.org},\n title = {Latent Geometry of Taste: Scalable Low-Rank Matrix Factorization for Recommender Systems},\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
