{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_15","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/sh -lc \"cat .codex/skills/scientific-evidence/spec.md 2>/dev/null || cat scientific-evidence/spec.md; sed -n '1,220p' .codex/skills/write-paper-standalone/scripts/validate_claims.py; cat .codex/skills/validate-paper/scripts/compile_latex.sh | head -110; sed -n '30,210p' results/ideas/02_cross_fitted_local_residual_medians/program_1/src/program.py\"","aggregated_output":"# scientific-evidence\n\nThis is the canonical generated spec bundle for the `scientific-evidence` skill.\nUse the skill script as the source of truth for schemas, layout, and wording.\n\n## Scope\n\nThis contract is generic and file-format-agnostic.\nIt supports inline evidence refs in text-like files, adjacent `.prov.json` sidecars for generated artifacts, and a central JSONL ledger.\n\n## Why this exists\n\nThe point of `scientific-evidence` is to make an agent leave a machine-checkable trail for important numbers, figures, tables, and derived outputs.\nA paper or report should not depend on free-form prose alone when those claims can point back to real artifacts.\nAlways use this contract during paper writing whenever the agent adds manuscript numbers, table values, figure inputs, or derived statistics.\n\n## Fixed directory structure\n\n```text\nscientific-evidence/\n  spec.md\n  bundle.manifest.json\n  ledger.jsonl\n  schemas/\n    evidence-reference.schema.json\n    artifact-manifest.schema.json\n    ledger-entry.schema.json\n    verification-report.schema.json\n```\n\nAgents should use this layout exactly. Do not invent alternate bundle directories.\n\n## Grammar\n\n```text\nEvidenceRef   := '@evidence[[' Target [ '#' Locator ] ']]'\nTarget        := non-empty path | absolute path | URI | stable identifier\nLocator       := opaque fragment without closing ']]'\nSidecar       := '<artifact>.prov.json'\nLedger        := 'scientific-evidence/ledger.jsonl'\n```\n\n### Notes\n\n- `Target` stays generic. The verifier may classify it as `path`, `absolute-path`, `uri`, `id`, or `unknown`.\n- `Locator` is opaque unless a verifier adapter knows how to interpret it.\n- Text-like artifacts should use inline `@evidence[[...]]` refs. Binary or generated outputs should carry an adjacent `.prov.json` sidecar.\n\n### Minimal examples\n\n- `@evidence[[TARGET]]`\n- `@evidence[[TARGET#LOCATOR]]`\n- `figure.png.prov.json`\n\n## Verification behavior\n\nA verifier uses this bundle to inspect whether the agent left a connected evidence trail.\nThe base verifier uses three reference states:\n\n- `resolved`: the target exists and the verifier can validate the locator semantics it understands.\n- `anchored`: the target exists, but only path/hash checks were possible or the locator remained opaque.\n- `dangling`: the target does not resolve, the sidecar chain breaks, or the reference is malformed.\n\n### Minimum verifier expectations\n\n1. Resolve every inline evidence ref to a target path, URI, or id when possible.\n2. Mark each ref as `resolved`, `anchored`, or `dangling`.\n3. For manifests, require every `derived_from` edge to resolve to at least `anchored`.\n4. When hashes are recorded, compare them. Missing hashes are allowed.\n5. Do not pretend to interpret unknown locator grammars. Keep them `anchored` unless an adapter proves more.\n\n### What verification should prove\n\nAt a minimum, a downstream verifier should be able to:\n\n- scan text-like artifacts for `@evidence[[...]]` refs\n- read `.prov.json` sidecars for generated artifacts\n- resolve refs against real files or stable ids\n- classify each link as `resolved`, `anchored`, or `dangling`\n- fail when a generated artifact has no input trail or when a claimed source does not exist\n\nThis does not prove every scientific claim automatically. It proves whether the agent left enough structure for later auditing and stricter replay.\nA core paper-writing policy is: do not hardcode result numbers inside plotting or calculation scripts when those values should come from real artifacts. Read from files and leave matching `@evidence[[...]]` refs near the read or derivation logic.\n\n## Schema set\n\nThe generated bundle includes:\n\n- `schemas/evidence-reference.schema.json`\n- `schemas/artifact-manifest.schema.json`\n- `schemas/ledger-entry.schema.json`\n- `schemas/verification-report.schema.json`\n- `spec.md`\n- `bundle.manifest.json`\n- `ledger.jsonl`\n\n### Schema intent\n\n- `evidence-reference`: parsed form of one inline `@evidence[[...]]` token.\n- `artifact-manifest`: canonical sidecar schema for `<artifact>.prov.json`.\n- `ledger-entry`: one JSONL row in `scientific-evidence/ledger.jsonl`.\n- `verification-report`: verifier output with per-reference results and summary counts.\n\n## Examples across file formats\n\n### Python\n\n```python\n# Read the metric from disk; do not hardcode 96.7 here.\n# @evidence[[results/metrics.json#mnist.accuracy_mean]]\nimport json\npayload = json.loads(open(\"results/metrics.json\", encoding=\"utf-8\").read())\nvalue = payload[\"mnist\"][\"accuracy_mean\"]\n```\n\n### Bash\n\n```bash\n# @evidence[[results/run_summary.csv#row(dataset=mnist,variant=proposed).accuracy]]\npython scripts/summarize_results.py --input results/run_summary.csv\n```\n\n### LaTeX\n\n```tex\nAccuracy reached 96.7\\%. % @evidence[[generated/stats.json#mnist.accuracy_mean]]\n```\n\n### Markdown\n\n```md\nMain result: 96.7%. <!-- @evidence[[generated/stats.json#mnist.accuracy_mean]] -->\n```\n\n### R\n\n```r\n# @evidence[[results/summary.tsv#humanoid.edppo.mean]]\nsummary <- read.delim(\"results/summary.tsv\")\nvalue <- subset(summary, method == \"ED-PPO\" & env == \"Humanoid\")$mean[[1]]\n```\n\n### YAML\n\n```yaml\n# @evidence[[generated/stats.json#mnist.accuracy_mean]]\nreported_metric: mnist_accuracy_mean\n```\n\n### JSON sidecar\n\n```json\n{\n  \"schema_name\": \"scientific-evidence.artifact-manifest\",\n  \"artifact\": {\"path\": \"figures/main.png\", \"kind\": \"figure\"},\n  \"derived_from\": [\n    \"@evidence[[generated/stats.json#mnist.accuracy_mean]]\",\n    \"@evidence[[scripts/build_figure.py]]\"\n  ]\n}\n```\n\n## Conventions\n\n- Prefer paths relative to the scientific-evidence root when practical.\n- Put workflow-specific detail in `payload` or `named_outputs` rather than mutating the base schema.\n- Generate this bundle with the skill script instead of hand-writing downstream copies.\n\n_Generated from scientific-evidence._\n#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"Validate generated claim-grounding artifacts before paper finalization.\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport argparse\nimport json\nimport os\nimport re\nimport stat\nimport subprocess\nimport sys\nimport tempfile\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom typing import Any\n\nKEY_RE = re.compile(r\"@\\w+\\{([^,]+),\")\nEVIDENCE_REF_RE = re.compile(r\"@evidence\\[\\[[^\\]]+\\]\\]\")\nTEX_INPUT_RE = re.compile(\n    r\"\\\\(?:input|include)(?![A-Za-z@])\\s*\"\n    r\"(?:\\{(?P<braced>[^{}]+)\\}|(?P<unbraced>[^\\s%{}]+))\"\n)\nTEX_IMPORT_COMMAND_RE = re.compile(r\"\\\\(?:input|include)(?![A-Za-z@])\")\nTEX_LOCAL_SUPPORT_RE = re.compile(\n    r\"\\\\(?P<command>usepackage|RequirePackage|documentclass|LoadClass)\"\n    r\"(?![A-Za-z@])(?:\\s*\\[[^\\]]*\\])?\\s*\\{(?P<targets>[^{}]+)\\}\"\n)\nTEX_LOCAL_SUPPORT_COMMAND_RE = re.compile(\n    r\"\\\\(?:usepackage|RequirePackage|documentclass|LoadClass)(?![A-Za-z@])\"\n)\nDYNAMIC_TEX_IMPORT_RE = re.compile(r\"\\\\csname\\s*(?:input|include)\\s*\\\\endcsname\")\nCONDITIONAL_TOKEN_RE = re.compile(r\"\\\\if[a-zA-Z@]+\\b|\\\\else\\b|\\\\fi\\b\")\nVERBATIM_ENV_RE = re.compile(\n    r\"\\\\begin\\s*\\{(?P<env>verbatim\\*?|lstlisting|minted)\\}.*?\"\n    r\"\\\\end\\s*\\{(?P=env)\\}\",\n    re.DOTALL,\n)\nPROMPT_ARTIFACT_RE = re.compile(r\".+_prompt(?:_round_\\d+(?:_contract_retry_\\d+)?)?\\.md$\")\nGENERATED_EVIDENCE_SCAN_ARTIFACT_NAMES = {\n    \"validation_feedback.json\",\n    \"validation_feedback.md\",\n    \"verification-report.json\",\n}\nROOT_GENERATED_EVIDENCE_SCAN_ARTIFACT_NAMES = {\"validation_report.json\"}\nGENERATED_EVIDENCE_SCAN_ARTIFACT_PREFIXES = (\n    \"paper_evidence_audit\",\n)\nEVIDENCE_BUNDLE_DIRNAME = \"scientific-evidence\"\nEVIDENCE_SCAN_SUFFIXES = (\n    \".tex\",\n    \".md\",\n    \".json\",\n    \".yaml\",\n    \".yml\",\n    \".py\",\n    \".sh\",\n    \".r\",\n    \".csv\",\n    \".tsv\",\n)\nEVIDENCE_SKIP_DIR_NAMES = {\n    \".git\",\n    \"__pycache__\",\n    EVIDENCE_BUNDLE_DIRNAME,\n}\nAGENT_SKILL_DIR_PREFIXES = (\n    (\".claude\", \"skills\"),\n    (\".codex\", \"skills\"),\n    (\".cursor\", \"skills\"),\n    (\".opencode\", \"skills\"),\n    (\".gemini\", \"skills\"),\n    (\".pi\", \"agent\", \"skills\"),\n)\nVERIFICATION_SUMMARY_KEYS = (\n    \"total_references\",\n    \"resolved_references\",\n    \"anchored_references\",\n    \"dangling_references\",\n    \"manifests_checked\",\n)\nSCIENTIFIC_EVIDENCE_SCRIPT = (\n    Path(__file__).resolve().parent.parent.parent\n    / \"scientific-evidence\"\n    / \"scripts\"\n    / \"scientific_evidence.py\"\n)\n\n\ndef read_json(path: Path) -> dict[str, Any]:\n    \"\"\"Read JSON data from disk when available.\"\"\"\n    try:\n        payload = json.loads(path.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\"))\n    except json.JSONDecodeError as exc:\n        raise SystemExit(f\"Invalid JSON in {path}: {exc}\") from exc\n    if not isinstance(payload, dict):\n        raise SystemExit(f\"Expected JSON object in {path}\")\n    return payload\n\n\ndef read_bib_keys(path: Path) -> set[str]:\n    \"\"\"Read bib keys.\"\"\"\n    text = path.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\")\n    return {match.group(1).strip() for match in KEY_RE.finditer(text) if match.group(1).strip()}\n\n\ndef validate_reference_provenance(*, references_payload: dict[str, Any], bib_keys: set[str]) -> tuple[set[str], list[str]]:\n    \"\"\"Validate references_provenance.json against references.bib.\"\"\"\n    errors: list[str] = []\n    refs = references_payload.get(\"references\")\n    if not isinstance(refs, list):\n        return set(), [\"references_provenance.json must contain a `references` list.\"]\n\n    provenance_keys: set[str] = set()\n    provenance_ids: set[str] = set()\n    for idx, row in enumerate(refs):\n        if not isinstance(row, dict):\n            errors.append(f\"references[{idx}] must be object\")\n            continue\n        source_id = row.get(\"id\")\n        if not isinstance(source_id, str) or not source_id.strip():\n            errors.append(f\"references[{idx}].id missing\")\n        else:\n            if source_id in provenance_ids:\n                errors.append(f\"references[{idx}].id duplicates existing id: {source_id!r}\")\n            provenance_ids.add(source_id)\n\n        citation_key = row.get(\"citation_key\")\n        if not isinstance(citation_key, str) or not citation_key.strip():\n            errors.append(f\"references[{idx}].citation_key missing\")\n            continue\n        if citation_key in provenance_keys:\n            errors.append(\n                f\"references[{idx}].citation_key duplicates existing key: {citation_key!r}\"\n            )\n        provenance_keys.add(citation_key)\n\n    missing_in_provenance = sorted(bib_keys - provenance_keys)\n    if missing_in_provenance:\n        errors.append(\n            \"references.bib keys missing from references_provenance.json: \"\n            + \", \".join(repr(key) for key in missing_in_provenance)\n        )\n\n    missing_in_bib = sorted(provenance_keys - bib_keys)\n    if missing_in_bib:\n        errors.append(\n            \"references_provenance.json keys missing from references.bib: \"\n            + \", \".join(repr(key) for key in missing_in_bib)\n        )\n\n    return provenance_ids, errors\n\n\ndef is_excluded_evidence_scan_path(path: Path, *, paper_dir: Path) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Return True for operational artifacts that should not enter evidence scans.\"\"\"\n    rel_parts = path.relative_to(paper_dir).parts\n    if any(rel_parts[: len(prefix)] == prefix for prefix in AGENT_SKILL_DIR_PREFIXES):\n        return True\n    if any(part in EVIDENCE_SKIP_DIR_NAMES for part in rel_parts):\n        return True\n    if len(rel_parts) == 1 and rel_parts[0] in ROOT_GENERATED_EVIDENCE_SCAN_ARTIFACT_NAMES:\n        return True\n    if path.name in GENERATED_EVIDENCE_SCAN_ARTIFACT_NAMES:\n        return True\n    if any(path.name.startswith(prefix) for prefix in GENERATED_EVIDENCE_SCAN_ARTIFACT_PREFIXES):\n        return True\n    return bool(PROMPT_ARTIFACT_RE.fullmatch(path.name))\n\n\ndef strip_tex_comments(tex_text: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Remove LaTeX comments while preserving escaped percent signs.\"\"\"\n    cleaned_lines: list[str] = []\n    for line in tex_text.splitlines():\n        comment_at = len(line)\n        index = 0\n        while index < len(line):\n            if line.startswith(r\"\\verb\", index):\n                delimiter_index = index + len(r\"\\verb\")\n                if delimiter_index < len(line) and line[delimiter_index] == \"*\":\n                    delimiter_index += 1\n                if (\n                    delimiter_index < len(line)\n                    and not line[delimiter_index].isspace()\n                    and not line[delimiter_index].isalpha()\n                ):\n                    closing_index = line.find(line[delimiter_index], delimiter_index + 1)\n                    if closing_index >= 0:\n                        index = closing_index + 1\n                        continue\n            char = line[index]\n            if char != \"%\":\n                index += 1\n                continue\n            backslashes = 0\n            cursor = index - 1\n            while cursor >= 0 and line[cursor] == \"\\\\\":\n                backslashes += 1\n                cursor -= 1\n            if backslashes % 2 == 0:\n                comment_at = index\n                break\n            index += 1\n        cleaned_lines.append(line[:comment_at])\n    return \"\\n\".join(cleaned_lines)\n\n\ndef strip_false_conditionals(tex_text: str) -> str:\n    r\"\"\"Remove literal ``\\iffalse ... \\fi`` regions before dependency parsing.\"\"\"\n    output: list[str] = []\n    cursor = 0\n    while (false_match := re.search(r\"\\\\iffalse\\b\", tex_text[cursor:])) is not None:\n        false_start = cursor + false_match.start()\n        output.append(tex_text[cursor:false_start])\n        depth = 1\n        false_end = len(tex_text)\n        else_start: int | None = None\n        closing_start = len(tex_text)\n        for token in CONDITIONAL_TOKEN_RE.finditer(tex_text, false_start + len(r\"\\iffalse\")):\n            token_text = token.group(0).lower()\n            if token_text == r\"\\fi\":\n#!/bin/bash\nset -euo pipefail\n\nif [ $# -ne 1 ]; then\n  echo \"Usage: bash compile_latex.sh <paper.tex>\" >&2\n  exit 2\nfi\n\nTEX_ARGUMENT=\"$1\"\nif [ ! -f \"$TEX_ARGUMENT\" ]; then\n  echo \"Missing TeX file: $TEX_ARGUMENT\" >&2\n  exit 2\nfi\n\nif ! command -v pdflatex >/dev/null 2>&1; then\n  echo \"Missing required command: pdflatex\" >&2\n  exit 2\nfi\nif ! command -v bibtex >/dev/null 2>&1; then\n  echo \"Missing required command: bibtex\" >&2\n  exit 2\nfi\nif ! command -v python3 >/dev/null 2>&1; then\n  echo \"Missing required command: python3\" >&2\n  exit 2\nfi\nif ! command -v pdftotext >/dev/null 2>&1; then\n  echo \"Missing required command: pdftotext\" >&2\n  exit 2\nfi\n\nSCRIPT_DIR=\"$(cd \"$(dirname \"$0\")\" && pwd)\"\nPAPER_DIR=\"$(cd \"$(dirname \"$TEX_ARGUMENT\")\" && pwd)\"\nTEX_FILE=\"$(basename \"$TEX_ARGUMENT\")\"\nBASE=\"${TEX_FILE%.tex}\"\nRECORDER_FILE=\"${BASE}.fls\"\nAUX_FILE=\"${BASE}.aux\"\n\ncd \"$PAPER_DIR\"\n\nrun_sanitized() {\n  python3 \"$SCRIPT_DIR/validate_compile_inputs.py\" run -- \"$@\"\n}\n\nrun_pdflatex() {\n  rm -f -- \"$RECORDER_FILE\"\n  set +e\n  run_sanitized pdflatex \\\n    -recorder -no-shell-escape -interaction=nonstopmode -halt-on-error \"$TEX_FILE\"\n  local return_code=$?\n  set -e\n  if [ -f \"$RECORDER_FILE\" ]; then\n    python3 \"$SCRIPT_DIR/validate_compile_inputs.py\" recorder \\\n      --paper-dir \"$PAPER_DIR\" --fls \"$RECORDER_FILE\"\n  elif [ \"$return_code\" -eq 0 ]; then\n    echo \"LaTeX recorder output missing: $PAPER_DIR/$RECORDER_FILE\" >&2\n    return 1\n  fi\n  return \"$return_code\"\n}\n\nrun_pdflatex\npython3 \"$SCRIPT_DIR/validate_compile_inputs.py\" bibtex \\\n  --paper-dir \"$PAPER_DIR\" --aux \"$AUX_FILE\"\nrun_sanitized bibtex \"$BASE\"\nrun_pdflatex\nrun_pdflatex\npython3 \"$SCRIPT_DIR/validate_rendered_si.py\" --pdf \"${BASE}.pdf\"\n{\"predictions\": [N finite floats in [0,1]]}. Predictions cover ALL N columns, including\nunobserved ones; target membership and masks are never disclosed. Predict must not\nconsume future observations. A new begin discards the preceding trajectory state.\n\nThe same operations/settings apply in reduced smoke and all production workloads.\nEvaluator-owned constant-history, independent-column permutation, constant/copy\nbaselines, and reset replay test this actual implementation under matched budgets.\nControls have no required direction of error change; null findings are legitimate.\nNo state flags, self-reported metrics, file outputs or undocumented response keys.\nNo adaptivity restriction: selection may be nonadaptive; inference uses observations.\nEach complete JSON message must be strictly below 64 MiB (chunks target below 8 MiB).\n\"\"\"\nimport base64\nimport math\n\nimport numpy as np\n\n\n_state = {}\n\n\ndef _fit_residual_base(values, mask, rank, ridge, sweeps, rng):\n    rank = min(rank, *values.shape)\n    counts = mask.sum(axis=0)\n    means = np.divide((values * mask).sum(axis=0), counts,\n                      out=np.full(values.shape[1], 0.5), where=counts > 0)\n    centered = values - means\n    factors = rng.normal(0, .1, size=(values.shape[1], rank))\n    latent = np.zeros((values.shape[0], rank))\n    identity = ridge * np.eye(rank)\n    for sweep in range(sweeps):\n        for row in range(values.shape[0]):\n            design = factors[mask[row]]\n            latent[row] = np.linalg.solve(identity + design.T @ design,\n                                          design.T @ centered[row, mask[row]])\n        for column in range(values.shape[1]):\n            design = latent[mask[:, column]]\n            factors[column] = np.linalg.solve(identity + design.T @ design,\n                                              design.T @ centered[mask[:, column], column])\n    variance = np.divide((centered * centered * mask).sum(axis=0), counts,\n                         out=np.zeros(values.shape[1]), where=counts > 0)\n    return dict(means=means, factors=factors, ridge=ridge,\n                scales=np.maximum(np.sqrt(variance), 0.025))\n\n\ndef _condition_base(model, selected_indices, observed_scores):\n    factors, means = model['factors'], model['means']\n    design = factors[selected_indices]\n    latent = np.linalg.solve(model['ridge'] * np.eye(factors.shape[1]) + design.T @ design,\n                             design.T @ (np.asarray(observed_scores) - means[selected_indices]))\n    return np.clip(means + factors @ latent, 0, 1)\n\n\ndef _policy_index(model, selected_indices, available):\n    factors = model['factors']\n    covariance = np.linalg.inv(model['ridge'] * np.eye(factors.shape[1])\n                               + factors[selected_indices].T @ factors[selected_indices])\n    cross = factors @ covariance @ factors[available].T\n    denominator = 1 + np.sum((factors[available] @ covariance) * factors[available], axis=1)\n    gains = np.sum(cross * cross, axis=0) / denominator\n    return int(available[int(np.argmax(gains))])\n\n\ndef _donor_predictions(model, donor_scores, selected_indices):\n    predictions = np.broadcast_to(model['means'], donor_scores.shape).copy()\n    anchor_scores = donor_scores[:, selected_indices]\n    anchor_mask = np.isfinite(anchor_scores)\n    patterns, pattern_ids = np.unique(anchor_mask, axis=0, return_inverse=True)\n    for pattern_index, pattern in enumerate(patterns):\n        donor_indices = np.flatnonzero(pattern_ids == pattern_index)\n        if not pattern.any():\n            continue\n        anchors = np.asarray(selected_indices, dtype=int)[pattern]\n        design = model['factors'][anchors]\n        responses = anchor_scores[donor_indices][:, pattern] - model['means'][anchors]\n        latent = np.linalg.solve(model['ridge'] * np.eye(design.shape[1]) + design.T @ design,\n                                 design.T @ responses.T)\n        predictions[donor_indices] += latent.T @ model['factors'].T\n    return np.clip(predictions, 0, 1)\n\n\ndef _build_residual_bank(values, mask, pool_rows, inner_validation_rows,\n                         rank, ridge, sweeps, rng):\n    \"\"\"Every donor is excluded from its fit, including within nested validation.\"\"\"\n    donor_pool = rng.permutation(pool_rows)[:128]\n    folds = []\n    for donor_rows in np.array_split(donor_pool, 2):\n        fit_rows = np.setdiff1d(pool_rows, donor_rows)\n        assert np.intersect1d(inner_validation_rows, fit_rows).size == 0\n        assert np.intersect1d(inner_validation_rows, donor_rows).size == 0\n        assert np.intersect1d(fit_rows, donor_rows).size == 0\n        if donor_rows.size == 0 or fit_rows.size == 0:\n            continue\n        model = _fit_residual_base(values[fit_rows], mask[fit_rows], rank, ridge, sweeps, rng)\n        donor_scores = np.where(mask[donor_rows], values[donor_rows], np.nan)\n        folds.append(dict(model=model, scores=donor_scores))\n    if not folds:\n        return None\n    return dict(folds=folds, scores=np.concatenate([fold['scores'] for fold in folds]), cache={})\n\n\ndef _bank_residuals(bank, selected_indices):\n    key = tuple(selected_indices)\n    if key not in bank['cache']:\n        donor_target_scores = bank['scores']\n        donor_base_predictions = np.concatenate([\n            _donor_predictions(fold['model'], fold['scores'], selected_indices)\n            for fold in bank['folds']])\n        donor_residuals = donor_target_scores - donor_base_predictions\n        usable_donors = np.isfinite(donor_target_scores) & np.isfinite(donor_base_predictions)\n        donor_residuals[~usable_donors] = np.nan\n        if len(bank['cache']) >= 8:\n            del bank['cache'][next(iter(bank['cache']))]\n        bank['cache'][key] = donor_residuals\n    return bank['cache'][key]\n\n\ndef _profile_weights(donor_anchor_scores, observed_anchor_scores, anchor_scales,\n                      selected_indices, bandwidth):\n    common_mask = np.isfinite(donor_anchor_scores) & np.isfinite(observed_anchor_scores)[None, :]\n    overlap_count = common_mask.sum(axis=1)\n    differences = np.where(common_mask, donor_anchor_scores - observed_anchor_scores[None, :], 0.0)\n    squared_distance = np.sum((differences / anchor_scales) ** 2, axis=1)\n    squared_distance /= np.maximum(overlap_count, 1)\n    neighbor_weights = np.exp(-0.5 * squared_distance / bandwidth ** 2)\n    neighbor_weights *= overlap_count / max(len(selected_indices), 1)\n    neighbor_weights[overlap_count == 0] = 0.0\n    return neighbor_weights\n\n\ndef _bank_weights(bank, selected_indices, observed_anchor_scores, bandwidth):\n    return np.concatenate([\n        _profile_weights(fold['scores'][:, selected_indices], observed_anchor_scores,\n                         fold['model']['scales'][selected_indices], selected_indices, bandwidth)\n        for fold in bank['folds']])\n\n\ndef _weighted_median(residuals, weights):\n    order = np.argsort(residuals, kind='stable')\n    sorted_residuals, sorted_weights = residuals[order], weights[order]\n    median_index = np.searchsorted(np.cumsum(sorted_weights), 0.5 * sorted_weights.sum(), side=\"left\")\n    return sorted_residuals[min(median_index, len(sorted_residuals) - 1)]\n\n\ndef _correct_target(base_prediction, residuals, target_weights, blend_strength, shrinkage_strength):\n    weight_floor = 1e-12\n    if target_weights.sum() <= weight_floor: return base_prediction\n    effective_neighbors = target_weights.sum() ** 2 / max(np.dot(target_weights, target_weights), weight_floor)\n    residual_correction = _weighted_median(residuals, target_weights)\n    correction_weight = blend_strength * effective_neighbors / (effective_neighbors + shrinkage_strength)\n    prediction = base_prediction + correction_weight * residual_correction\n    return prediction\n\n\ndef _residual_summaries(donor_residuals, neighbor_weights):\n    columns = donor_residuals.shape[1]\n    medians, effective_counts = np.zeros(columns), np.zeros(columns)\n    for target in range(columns):\n        usable = np.isfinite(donor_residuals[:, target]) & (neighbor_weights > 0)\n        target_weights = neighbor_weights[usable]\n        weight_sum = target_weights.sum()\n        if weight_sum <= 1e-12:\n            continue\n        medians[target] = _weighted_median(donor_residuals[usable, target], target_weights)\n        effective_counts[target] = weight_sum ** 2 / max(np.dot(target_weights, target_weights), 1e-12)\n    return medians, effective_counts\n\n\ndef _prepare_residual_correction(values, mask, rank, ridge, sweeps, seed):\n    \"\"\"Bounded nested historical calibration; never receives a new-model score.\n\n    Predeclared local grid: bandwidth (.35, .75, 1.5), shrinkage (4, 16),\n    blend (0, .25, .5, 1). At most 512 rows / approximately 196608 cells,\n    128 donors, 16 validation rows, two outer folds and two donor folds.\n    Auxiliary ALS fits use at most 12 sweeps; the incumbent fit is untouched.\n    Validation compares all methods on the same finite unqueried cells at\n    budgets 1, 2, 4, 8. Diagnostic results are private, not RPC extensions.\n    \"\"\"\n    candidate_blends = (0.0, 0.25, 0.5, 1.0)\n    candidate_bandwidths = (0.35, 0.75, 1.5)\n    candidate_shrinkages = (4.0, 16.0)\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
