{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_36","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/sh -lc \"sed -n '1,180p' task/program_0/src/program.py; sed -n '870,904p' task/evaluate_final.py; cat .codex/skills/validate-paper/scripts/compile_latex.sh | head -85; cat .codex/skills/validate-paper/scripts/validate_figures.py | head -75; python - <<'PY'\nimport json\np=json.load(open('task/resources/final/plan.json'))\nprint('plan',[(e['case'],e['seed'],len(e['history']),len(e['test']),e['replay']) for e in p['episodes']]); print('manifest', {k:v for k,v in json.load(open('task/resources/final/manifest.json')).items() if k in ['revision','source_row_count','model_count','column_count','cross_plane_disjoint']})\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"\"\"\"CPU score-matrix prediction starter; only handle(request) is public.\n\nAll requests/responses are finite JSON objects. Additional response keys are forbidden.\nAll indices are zero-based, episode-local and opaque; no filenames or model IDs are used.\nreset accepts ANY nonnegative integer seed and returns exactly {\"ok\": true}; it clears\nall state. Seeds initialize randomness, never choose a workload or evaluation plane.\n\nHistory upload (one per episode): upload_start fields shape=[M,N], dtype=\"float64\",\nbyteorder=\"little\", mask_dtype=\"uint8\", encoding=\"base64\", layout=\"values_then_mask\",\nnbytes=9*M*N, chunks=C. Bounds: 1<=M,N<=4096, 1<=C<=64, <=256 MiB logical data.\nReturns {\"ok\": true}. upload_chunk fields index (sequential 0..C-1) and data (base64\nstring, <=4 MiB decoded). Returns {\"ok\": true}. upload_commit has no other fields,\nreturns {\"ok\": true}. Bytes are contiguous little-endian float64 [M,N] values then\nuint8 [M,N] observed mask, row major. Missing entries are zero with mask=0. Scores\nhave already been normalized by public metric ranges to [0,1]. Buffers are private\nmemory, never shared files. At most one upload is live; outstanding transfer <=512 MiB.\n\nfit fields rank (positive integer <=16), sweeps (positive integer <=50), ridge\n(positive float). Returns {\"ok\": true}. These are requested settings, not scientific\nevidence of internal computation. Training uses history only. Fit/preprocessing must\nremain immutable until reset; no observations from new models may enter history.\n\nbegin fields trajectory (nonnegative int), queryable (distinct integer indices in\n0..N-1, at least eight), budget=8. Returns {\"ok\": true}. Clears only the current\nnew-model observations, never fitted history. select has no other fields; returns\nexactly {\"index\": int}, an available not-yet-selected queryable index. observe fields\nindex (the most recently selected index) and value (finite [0,1] score); returns\n{\"ok\": true}. Only that score is authorized feedback. select/observe repeats eight\ntimes; predict is called after 1,2,4,8 observations and returns exactly\n{\"predictions\": [N finite floats in [0,1]]}. Predictions cover ALL N columns, including\nunobserved ones; target membership and masks are never disclosed. Predict must not\nconsume future observations. A new begin discards the preceding trajectory state.\n\nThe same operations/settings apply in reduced smoke and all production workloads.\nEvaluator-owned constant-history, independent-column permutation, constant/copy\nbaselines, and reset replay test this actual implementation under matched budgets.\nControls have no required direction of error change; null findings are legitimate.\nNo state flags, self-reported metrics, file outputs or undocumented response keys.\nNo adaptivity restriction: selection may be nonadaptive; inference uses observations.\nEach complete JSON message must be strictly below 64 MiB (chunks target below 8 MiB).\n\"\"\"\nimport base64\nimport math\n\nimport numpy as np\n\n\n_state = {}\n\n\ndef handle(request):\n    operation = request['op']\n    if operation == 'reset':\n        seed = request['seed']\n        if type(seed) is not int or seed < 0:\n            raise ValueError('invalid seed')\n        _state.clear()\n        _state['rng'] = np.random.default_rng(seed)\n        return {'ok': True}\n    if operation == 'upload_start':\n        rows, columns = request['shape']\n        if (any(type(count) is not int or not 1 <= count <= 4096 for count in [rows, columns])\n                or request['nbytes'] != 9 * rows * columns or request['nbytes'] > 256 * 1024**2\n                or not 1 <= request['chunks'] <= 64\n                or [request[key] for key in ['dtype', 'byteorder', 'mask_dtype', 'encoding', 'layout']]\n                != ['float64', 'little', 'uint8', 'base64', 'values_then_mask']):\n            raise ValueError('invalid upload')\n        _state['upload'] = bytearray()\n        _state['metadata'] = dict(request)\n        _state['next_chunk'] = 0\n        return {'ok': True}\n    if operation == 'upload_chunk':\n        metadata = _state['metadata']\n        if request['index'] != _state['next_chunk'] or request['index'] >= metadata['chunks']:\n            raise ValueError('invalid chunk order')\n        decoded = base64.b64decode(request['data'], validate=True)\n        if len(decoded) > 4 * 1024**2 or len(_state['upload']) + len(decoded) > metadata['nbytes']:\n            raise ValueError('invalid chunk size')\n        _state['upload'].extend(decoded)\n        _state['next_chunk'] += 1\n        return {'ok': True}\n    if operation == 'upload_commit':\n        metadata = _state['metadata']\n        if len(_state['upload']) != metadata['nbytes'] or _state['next_chunk'] != metadata['chunks']:\n            raise ValueError('incomplete upload')\n        rows, columns = metadata['shape']\n        count = rows * columns\n        _state['values'] = np.frombuffer(_state['upload'], dtype='<f8', count=count).reshape(rows, columns).copy()\n        _state['mask'] = np.frombuffer(_state['upload'], dtype='u1', offset=8*count).reshape(rows, columns).copy()\n        if (not np.isfinite(_state['values']).all() or not np.isin(_state['mask'], [0, 1]).all()\n                or np.any((_state['values'] < 0) | (_state['values'] > 1))):\n            raise ValueError('invalid history')\n        del _state['upload']\n        return {'ok': True}\n    if operation == 'fit':\n        values, mask = _state['values'], _state['mask'].astype(bool)\n        rank = min(int(request['rank']), *values.shape)\n        ridge = float(request['ridge'])\n        sweeps = int(request['sweeps'])\n        if not 1 <= rank <= 16 or not 1 <= sweeps <= 50 or not math.isfinite(ridge) or ridge <= 0:\n            raise ValueError('invalid fitting settings')\n        counts = mask.sum(axis=0)\n        means = np.divide((values * mask).sum(axis=0), counts,\n                          out=np.full(values.shape[1], 0.5), where=counts > 0)\n        centered = values - means\n        factors = _state['rng'].normal(0, .1, size=(values.shape[1], rank))\n        latent = np.zeros((values.shape[0], rank))\n        identity = ridge * np.eye(rank)\n        for sweep in range(sweeps):\n            for row in range(values.shape[0]):\n                design = factors[mask[row]]\n                latent[row] = np.linalg.solve(identity + design.T @ design, design.T @ centered[row, mask[row]])\n            for column in range(values.shape[1]):\n                design = latent[mask[:, column]]\n                factors[column] = np.linalg.solve(identity + design.T @ design, design.T @ centered[mask[:, column], column])\n        _state.update(means=means, factors=factors, ridge=ridge)\n        return {'ok': True}\n    if operation == 'begin':\n        _state['available'] = sorted(request['queryable'])\n        _state['observed'] = []\n        _state['scores'] = []\n        _state['pending'] = None\n        return {'ok': True}\n    if operation == 'select':\n        factors = _state['factors']\n        observed = _state['observed']\n        available = [index for index in _state['available'] if index not in observed]\n        covariance = np.linalg.inv(_state['ridge'] * np.eye(factors.shape[1]) + factors[observed].T @ factors[observed])\n        cross = factors @ covariance @ factors[available].T\n        denominator = 1 + np.sum((factors[available] @ covariance) * factors[available], axis=1)\n        gains = np.sum(cross * cross, axis=0) / denominator\n        chosen = int(available[int(np.argmax(gains))])\n        _state['pending'] = chosen\n        return {'index': chosen}\n    if operation == 'observe':\n        if request['index'] != _state['pending']:\n            raise ValueError('observation without selection')\n        _state['observed'].append(request['index'])\n        _state['scores'].append(float(request['value']))\n        _state['pending'] = None\n        return {'ok': True}\n    if operation == 'predict':\n        factors, means = _state['factors'], _state['means']\n        observed = _state['observed']\n        design = factors[observed]\n        latent = np.linalg.solve(_state['ridge'] * np.eye(factors.shape[1]) + design.T @ design,\n                                 design.T @ (np.asarray(_state['scores']) - means[observed]))\n        return {'predictions': np.clip(means + factors @ latent, 0, 1).tolist()}\n    raise ValueError('unsupported operation')\ndef run_baseline(name, values, mask, tests, partitions_for_rows, seed, sweeps):\n    means = np.divide((values*mask).sum(axis=0), mask.sum(axis=0),\n                      out=np.full(values.shape[1], .5), where=mask.sum(axis=0) > 0)\n    factors = None\n    if name in ['random_low_rank', 'variance_low_rank']:\n        means, factors = fit_low_rank(values, mask, seed, sweeps)\n    variance = np.divide(((values-means)**2 * mask).sum(axis=0), mask.sum(axis=0),\n                         out=np.zeros(values.shape[1]), where=mask.sum(axis=0)>0)\n    losses = np.ones((len(tests), 4))\n    for row, (reservoir, target) in enumerate(partitions_for_rows):\n        if name == 'random_low_rank':\n            selection = np.random.default_rng(seed + row * 37).permutation(reservoir).tolist()[:8]\n        else:\n            selection = sorted(reservoir, key=lambda index: (-variance[index], index))[:8]\n        for checkpoint_index, budget in enumerate(CHECKPOINTS):\n            observed = selection[:budget]\n            if name == 'column_mean':\n                predicted = means\n            elif name == 'copy_skill':\n                predicted = np.full(len(means), tests[row, observed].mean())\n            elif name == 'linear_ridge':\n                design = np.where(mask[:, observed], values[:, observed]-means[observed], 0)\n                coefficients = np.linalg.solve(.1*np.eye(budget) + design.T@design,\n                                               design.T @ np.where(mask, values-means, 0))\n                predicted = np.clip(means + (tests[row, observed]-means[observed]) @ coefficients, 0, 1)\n            else:\n                design = factors[observed]\n                latent = np.linalg.solve(.1*np.eye(factors.shape[1]) + design.T@design,\n                                         design.T @ (tests[row, observed]-means[observed]))\n                predicted = np.clip(means + factors @ latent, 0, 1)\n            losses[row, checkpoint_index] = error_pair(predicted, tests[row], target)[0]\n    return losses\n\n\ndef worst_case(episode):\n#!/bin/bash\nset -euo pipefail\n\nif [ $# -ne 1 ]; then\n  echo \"Usage: bash compile_latex.sh <paper.tex>\" >&2\n  exit 2\nfi\n\nTEX_ARGUMENT=\"$1\"\nif [ ! -f \"$TEX_ARGUMENT\" ]; then\n  echo \"Missing TeX file: $TEX_ARGUMENT\" >&2\n  exit 2\nfi\n\nif ! command -v pdflatex >/dev/null 2>&1; then\n  echo \"Missing required command: pdflatex\" >&2\n  exit 2\nfi\nif ! command -v bibtex >/dev/null 2>&1; then\n  echo \"Missing required command: bibtex\" >&2\n  exit 2\nfi\nif ! command -v python3 >/dev/null 2>&1; then\n  echo \"Missing required command: python3\" >&2\n  exit 2\nfi\nif ! command -v pdftotext >/dev/null 2>&1; then\n  echo \"Missing required command: pdftotext\" >&2\n  exit 2\nfi\n\nSCRIPT_DIR=\"$(cd \"$(dirname \"$0\")\" && pwd)\"\nPAPER_DIR=\"$(cd \"$(dirname \"$TEX_ARGUMENT\")\" && pwd)\"\nTEX_FILE=\"$(basename \"$TEX_ARGUMENT\")\"\nBASE=\"${TEX_FILE%.tex}\"\nRECORDER_FILE=\"${BASE}.fls\"\nAUX_FILE=\"${BASE}.aux\"\n\ncd \"$PAPER_DIR\"\n\nrun_sanitized() {\n  python3 \"$SCRIPT_DIR/validate_compile_inputs.py\" run -- \"$@\"\n}\n\nrun_pdflatex() {\n  rm -f -- \"$RECORDER_FILE\"\n  set +e\n  run_sanitized pdflatex \\\n    -recorder -no-shell-escape -interaction=nonstopmode -halt-on-error \"$TEX_FILE\"\n  local return_code=$?\n  set -e\n  if [ -f \"$RECORDER_FILE\" ]; then\n    python3 \"$SCRIPT_DIR/validate_compile_inputs.py\" recorder \\\n      --paper-dir \"$PAPER_DIR\" --fls \"$RECORDER_FILE\"\n  elif [ \"$return_code\" -eq 0 ]; then\n    echo \"LaTeX recorder output missing: $PAPER_DIR/$RECORDER_FILE\" >&2\n    return 1\n  fi\n  return \"$return_code\"\n}\n\nrun_pdflatex\npython3 \"$SCRIPT_DIR/validate_compile_inputs.py\" bibtex \\\n  --paper-dir \"$PAPER_DIR\" --aux \"$AUX_FILE\"\nrun_sanitized bibtex \"$BASE\"\nrun_pdflatex\nrun_pdflatex\npython3 \"$SCRIPT_DIR/validate_rendered_si.py\" --pdf \"${BASE}.pdf\"\n#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"Validate figure manifest artifacts and basic figure readability budgets.\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport argparse\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nfrom src.orchestrator.paper_step import read_json, validate_figure_manifest\nfrom src.orchestrator.tex_graphics import read_tex_file_bounded\n\n\ndef parse_args() -> argparse.Namespace:\n    \"\"\"Parse command-line arguments.\"\"\"\n    parser = argparse.ArgumentParser(description=\"Validate figure manifest artifacts.\")\n    parser.add_argument(\"--paper-dir\", default=\".\")\n    return parser.parse_args()\n\n\ndef main() -> int:\n    \"\"\"Run the command-line entry point.\"\"\"\n    args = parse_args()\n    paper_dir = Path(args.paper_dir).resolve()\n    tex_path = paper_dir / \"paper.tex\"\n    paper_data_path = paper_dir / \"paper_data.json\"\n    references_path = paper_dir / \"references_provenance.json\"\n\n    if not tex_path.exists():\n        raise SystemExit(f\"Missing required artifact: {tex_path}\")\n\n    tex_text = read_tex_file_bounded(tex_path)\n    paper_data = read_json(paper_data_path)\n    references = read_json(references_path)\n    grounding_sources = paper_data.get(\"grounding_sources\")\n    if not isinstance(grounding_sources, dict):\n        raise SystemExit(\"paper_data missing grounding_sources object.\")\n    allowed_source_ids = set(str(key) for key in grounding_sources)\n    refs = references.get(\"references\")\n    if isinstance(refs, list):\n        for row in refs:\n            if isinstance(row, dict):\n                source_id = row.get(\"id\")\n                if isinstance(source_id, str) and source_id.strip():\n                    allowed_source_ids.add(source_id)\n\n    report = validate_figure_manifest(\n        paper_dir,\n        tex_text=tex_text,\n        allowed_source_ids=allowed_source_ids,\n    )\n    if not bool(report.get(\"checked\", False)):\n        print(\"No figures referenced or required; figure validation skipped.\")\n        return 0\n\n    hard_errors = report.get(\"hard_errors\", [])\n    if not isinstance(hard_errors, list):\n        raise SystemExit(\"figure_manifest validation returned invalid hard_errors payload\")\n    soft_warnings = report.get(\"soft_warnings\", [])\n    if not isinstance(soft_warnings, list):\n        raise SystemExit(\"figure_manifest validation returned invalid soft_warnings payload\")\n    if hard_errors:\n        raise SystemExit(\"Figure validation failed: \" + \"; \".join(str(error) for error in hard_errors))\n    if soft_warnings:\n        print(\"Figure validation warnings: \" + \"; \".join(str(message) for message in soft_warnings))\n\n    print(\n        f\"Validated {int(report.get('figure_count', 0))} figures with manifest and readability budgets.\"\n    )\n    return 0\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    raise SystemExit(main())\nplan [('A', 6841, 94, 32, False), ('B', 6841, 94, 32, False), ('C', 6841, 94, 32, False), ('D', 6841, 94, 32, False), ('A', 8089, 94, 32, False), ('B', 8089, 94, 32, False), ('C', 8089, 94, 32, False), ('D', 8089, 94, 32, False), ('A', 9011, 94, 32, False), ('B', 9011, 93, 33, False), ('C', 9011, 94, 32, False), ('D', 9011, 94, 32, False), ('A', 6841, 94, 32, True)]\nmanifest {'cross_plane_disjoint': True, 'revision': '6dabbcc68c28ea5f180ce7df79347b3ca9cc6383', 'source_row_count': 126}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
