{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_110","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/sh -lc \"rg 'author =|title =' references.bib; /tmp/apply_patch <<'PATCH'\n*** Begin Patch\n*** Update File: paper.tex\n@@\n-Across the three seeds, the package's pooled MAEs are 0.03850, 0.04113, and 0.04280, with descriptive sample standard deviation 0.00217. The corresponding linear-ridge values are 0.04166, 0.04594, and 0.04815. Each retained seeded aggregate favors the package, but the seeds reuse the same source matrix and overlapping components. They are not three independent dataset replications. The component-resampling construction gives reported bound minima of \"'$[0.00210,0.00920]$; the positive lower minimum supports the recorded aggregate comparison against each evaluated reference under that construction. Its upper endpoint need not refer to the same comparator as its lower endpoint.\n+The package'\"'s seed-level pooled MAEs are 0.03850, 0.04113, and 0.04280 (sample SD 0.00217), versus linear ridge's 0.04166, 0.04594, and 0.04815. These shared-data replications all favor the package. Component-bootstrap bound minima are \"'$[0.00210,0.00920]$. Their positive lower minimum supports the aggregate comparisons under the specified construction; the endpoints need not correspond to the same baseline.\n@@\n-The independent frozen evaluation completed and passed its qualification checks. The retained reset replay had identical query indices and maximum absolute prediction difference zero. These facts concern the evaluated protocol; they do not certify universal validity, absence of every form of leakage, or superiority outside these conditions. The manuscript uses evaluator-owned losses, not unverified predictor diagnostics. No new model evaluation is performed for this paper; all numerical displays are regenerated from retained final arrays.\n+The independent frozen evaluation completed and passed its qualification checks. Reset replay had identical query indices and maximum absolute prediction difference zero. These protocol checks do not certify universal validity or absence of every leakage source. Numerical displays use retained evaluator-owned losses, not unverified predictor diagnostics; no new model evaluation is performed for this paper.\n*** End Patch\nPATCH\npdflatex -recorder -no-shell-escape -interaction=nonstopmode -halt-on-error paper.tex > /tmp/paper_manual_compile.log 2>&1; tail -3 /tmp/paper_manual_compile.log'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
